# workers/pdf-render/.env.example — PDF worker container surface.
#
# Per-surface secret confinement (Phase 5 Step 8; Sec joint-review surface).
# This container holds EXACTLY ONE secret. The single-entry enumeration IS the
# security property — the zero-DB-isolation guarantee (Lock 13 mod #2) means a
# Postgres credential MUST NEVER appear here.
#
# Anchors (verified verbatim 2026-06-28):
#   - ADR-011 Lock 13 mod #2 — PDF worker zero-DB isolation: NO SUPABASE_* env
#     vars; NO Postgres client installed; the single permitted env var is
#     PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY per SD-20.
#   - ARCH §5 → PDF worker container: "ONLY PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY. NO SUPABASE_*
#     env vars; NO Postgres client ... installed in Dockerfile."
#   - SECURITY SD-20 / RT-21 — signed-JWT freshness battery.
#   - RT-22 CI fence (scripts/ci/fence-rt22-pdf-worker-dockerfile.sh) enforces the
#     credential/Postgres-client absence on workers/pdf-render/Dockerfile at PR-time.
#
# The PDF worker reaches the data layer ONLY via the V1 web-app's
# /internal/pdf-render endpoint under this short-lived signed JWT (Lock 13 mod #1).
# It has NO database reach by design. Adding ANY other secret here — especially a
# SUPABASE_* or Postgres credential — is a Lock 13 mod #2 violation and a
# Sec-veto one-way door.
#
# Secret-store assignment: PRODUCTION-ONLY (Coolify-injected on the V1 production
# VPS at deploy time — greenfield per ADR-021; the cax21/pfindash.com incumbent is
# reference-only, NOT the deploy target). The CI
# test analogue is the DISTINCT name PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY_TEST (manifest
# ci_only set) — never this production name.

# PDF worker JWT signing key — the worker's ONLY credential. Matches the V1
# web-app's PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY; used to mint/verify the /internal/pdf-render
# JWT (SD-20). NO database credentials accompany it, by design.
PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY=<pdf-worker-signing-key>
